  contentsAnswer: My sister is getting married. One suit, spare clothes, wash bag.
    Please tell me the suit survived.
  weightAnswer: Five or six kilos with the case. I had it on the airport scale.
  metalAnswer: Buckles and zips. I left the wedding gift in the car.
  packingAnswer: Clothes under the straps. Nothing switched on or loose.
  responseAnswer: That little tap? The handle, probably. There is nothing inside
    that should keep moving.
  authorReasoning: 'Innocent baseline: 5.4 kg, low metal, almost no pulse movement.
    A coherent everyday account.'
